WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome, guys.
-Thank you.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.635 line:92%
-I'm so happy to have you here.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to congratulate you
on the show.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
But first, Nafessa,
you are from Philadelphia.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:10.443
-I am born and raised in Philly,
and I'm celebrating all year.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.678 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Oh, that's fantastic.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.079 line:92%
You have to take the whole year.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.715
But you were not in Philadelphia
last night, correct?

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wasn't. I was here.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was, like, getting ready
for you today.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.520 line:92%
-Well, thank you for doing that.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.221 line:92%
-I had to have my fitting

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
and watch the Super Bowl
at the same time.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it was good. We won.
I'm good.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:24.858 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would feel bad,
but I have to be honest,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you schedule something,
you would never think,

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.598
"Well, that will be the day
the Eagles win the Super Bowl."

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
Never happened.
-No. No.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.968 size:78% position:39%
You can't plan that.
You can't predict it.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
Well, congratulations.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.037 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.139 size:75% position:38%
-The show is already
incredibly popular.

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is it
about the show that you feel

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:44.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
viewers are connecting with
so early in its run?

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.279 line:92%
-Well, I feel like the show,

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
even though it is about
a superhero

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.616 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and a superhero family,

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.317 line:92%
it's very rooted in reality.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, when it comes
to a superhero like Superman,

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.955 size:81% position:41% line:92%
it's very fantastical,

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you don't feel
like you can walk outside

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be like, "Ooh,
it's a bird, it's a plane."

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what I'm saying?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But with "Black Lightning,"
you feel like

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
you could see him
walking down the street.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Oh, there's our
neighborhood hero."

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:07.867
-Yeah, I think it's very
relatable, like she said.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.636 line:92%
He's a guy in your neighborhood.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.137 size:81% position:41% line:92%
He's the father figure

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you want within
the community,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:16.142
which makes it pretty authentic
and relatable.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.410 line:92%
-And it does use actual --

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.847 size:84% position:42%
I mean, it uses racism,
it uses gun violence.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that something
that drew it to --

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, again, I assume
when you first get a script

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you hear
it's about a comic book hero,

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
you might not expect
those things to be in there.

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.422 line:92%
Were you excited when they were?

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:32.258
-We were really, really
into the script when we read it.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
The female characters
are so strong

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.795 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and powerful, confident,

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
just boldly walking
in who they are.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.632
And, you know, those are the
kinds of roles that you want --

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.568
roles that are going to empower
and inspire.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the Akils, they have done
such a great job

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
of bringing that authenticity
to it.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:50.710
-Yeah, I love the fact the show
really tackles real issues.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
And The CW lets us
be unapologetically black.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:56.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
That's a good thing to be.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.252
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.121 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Snaps fingers ]

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.122 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Snap, snap, snap.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, have you had --
have you had

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.525 line:92%
great reactions from fans yet?

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.594 line:92%
Is there one that stands out?

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yes.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've had really great
fan reactions.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:14.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always love
the little kids that come up.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like,
"For Halloween,

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:16.603 line:92%
I want to be Black Lightning."

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, those are my favorites.
-Yeah.

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:19.372 line:92%
-Yeah, and I think for me,

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.208 size:78% position:39%
being the first black
lesbian superhero...

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:22.642 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...you know,
I'm getting a lot of

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
just outpour of love
and support of, you know,

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.580 line:92%
"Thank you for representing us.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
It took a while
for us to see ourselves."

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think representation
is really important,

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.218 line:92%
and we all need to be able

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
to turn on the television,
see ourselves,

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:34.854 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and be able to relate

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the characters
that we're watching.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:39.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, super honored to,
you know, be that voice.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's true,
I was not just --

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Aww. Thank you.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:47.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It feels like not just
black lesbian superheroes.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
There haven't been many
black lesbians on television.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:51.804
That must -- Did you feel
a responsibility to that,

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.541
or is it more like the freedom
of, "Oh, I get to do this thing

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:57.577
that not a lot of people have
seen and been able relate to"?

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:59.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, yeah,
I'm just really honored

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.681 size:78% position:39%
to give my voice over
and more so proud.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.482 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.050 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And hopefully this show,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.518 line:92%
or my character in particular,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.688
will be the first
of many black lesbians on film.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:10.857 line:92%
-And you had a background --

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:13.426
You did some criminal justice
stuff in Philadelphia, as well.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.695
-I did.
I interned at the D.A.'s office

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the homicide unit.
-Go ahead, girl!

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my goodness.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so I thought I wanted
to be a lawyer,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.634 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and then I told my mom,

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:22.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mom, I'm just gonna
play one on TV.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's -- That's the best
I can do for you."

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.072 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The things that I saw
within, you know,

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:29.809 line:92%
the criminal justice system

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.679
are very parallel to the things
that we're touching on,

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:33.880 line:92%
the topics within the show.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
So kudos to that experience,
I guess.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess a degree wasn't,
you know, a bad idea.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:39.552 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you have
a little background there.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:43.823
I'm guessing neither of you have
actual superhero backgrounds.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:47.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when it comes to stunts,
how is your stunt work?

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
And are you getting to do
some stunt work?

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:51.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I do a little bit
of butt kicking.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
My powers actually come
after hers.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.468
-Okay, gotcha, so --
-So I've been in stunt training

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.603 line:92%
since July, and it's been fun.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:59.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been pretty athletic
and active throughout my life,

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's just cool
to keep that going.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do as much
as my stunts as possible,

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:05.812
but my stunt double, Natasha,
she is really, really dope,

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:06.512 line:92%
and we have a lot of fun.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:09.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I can't wait for you guys
to see Thunder develop

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.150 line:92%
and really start kicking butt.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.252 line:92%
We're just getting started.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.386 line:92%
-Oh, that's very exciting.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've heard that
what you lack in stunts,

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:18.424
you make up for -- you do
a lot of running on set.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes.
-Oh, yes.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:22.095
-While she has a really amazing
workout routine,

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:25.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
my workout routine
is running from craft services

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
back to the set.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:27.367 line:92%
-You know what I'm saying?

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you run to get snacks.
-Exactly.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then
they're looking for you,

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.170 line:92%
and you have to run back.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they really try
to mess with me sometimes

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.575
because they put craft services
on a different stage.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:36.009 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, wow.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Then when we're filming,
I'll be like,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.578
"It's okay,
I'ma get my snacks either way."

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whenever they yell cut
and you're looking for China,

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.682 line:92%
crafty is where she's at.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:45.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And do you have
a favorite snack?

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you --
-Laffy Taffys.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:48.588 line:92%
And you guys had them backstage.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.056 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, we heard.

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:52.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
You like Laffy Taffy so much,
it got to us.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It made me really care
about you guys.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.031
I cared about you so much
when I walked in here.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:58.731 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Oh, well, thank you.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what we try
to do with our Laffy Taffy,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.467 line:92%
and I'm glad -- Once again,

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
Laffy Taffy brings
people together.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.504 line:92%
And congratulations, guys.

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really just lovely
meeting you both,

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
and continued best of luck
on the show.

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:09.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for having us.

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give it up
for China Anne McClain

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.545 line:92%
and Nafessa Williams, everybody!

